  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and SQ20B, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 8-methoxy-3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-7-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2S,3S,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxychromen-4-one, 2,3-Didehydroalanine, and 6-(2-hydroxypropanoyl)-4a,7-dihydro-1H-pteridine-2,4-dione. These compounds all share a common pathway of targeting the 26S proteasome subunit, which in turn leads to the activation of SQ20B. The scores for these relationships are consistent, indicating a potential role for Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside in modulating the proteasome activity, thereby influencing SQ20B. The evidence suggests that the relationship between the compound and SQ20B is mediated through the proteasome, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
